FILED s533b (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-03) from the port's D0 measurement (the requalifier's legacy home vs the binder's, over the four populations + the gate): the ONE new disagreement shape, core Encode.pm:184 and :196 (inside `if ($ON_EBCDIC) { package Encode::UTF_EBCDIC; ... sub decode { ... for ( my $i = 0 ; $i < length($str) ; $i++ ) ...`, dead code on this box).  FIXED BY THE PORT (s533b): the requalifier now asks the binder, whose `for (my $i = ...; ...; ...)` binding runs from the init to the end of the loop (perly.y:758 mnexpr).

REPRODUCER (probed vs perl 5.40.3; scratch/s533b/pr/CF.pl in the s533b worktree):

    sub run {
        package Q;
        my $s = "";
        for (my $i = 0; $i < 3; $i++) { $s .= $i }
        print "s=$s Q::i=", $Q::i // "u", "\n";
    }
    run();
    { package R; my $t = ""; for (my $j = 0; $j < 2; $j++) { $t .= $j } print "t=$t R::j=", $R::j // "u", "\n" }

perl:              s=012 Q::i=u / t=01 R::j=u
base 4fb60297:     s=000 Q::i=3 / t=00 R::j=2   -- SILENT WRONG: the loop's CONDITION and STEP read/write the package global $Q::i, the BODY reads the lexical (stuck at 0).

WHY (legacy): `_binding_at_0` climbed from the condition's `$i` through the Structure::For to the enclosing BLOCK and looked at the block's earlier statements and the block's own HEAD -- the C-style for's init `my` is inside the For structure, a sibling of the loop body, not an ancestor of the condition, so the condition and the step were answered "global" and requalified; the body's `$i` found the init through `_head_binding` and stayed lexical.


